// Conjure-compat wrapper machinery.
//
// Package choice: this joins the existing `nominal.run.v1` package rather than minting a v2. The ADR's "reshapes mint
// a v2 package" rule exists to guarantee non-collision with legacy Conjure paths when an already-shipped pattern-A
// package is reshaped. No RunService gRPC surface has ever shipped — `nominal.run.v1` holds only the shared value
// types (Unit, UtcTimestamp, WeakTimestampType) in run.proto, whose own `java_outer_classname` comment anticipates
// "the `Run` message added by run_service.proto in this same java package". Legacy Conjure run paths are rooted at
// `/scout/v1/...`, so the `/run/v1/...` mappings below collide with nothing; the not-shadowed tests in
// RunTranscodeIntegrationTest are the enforcement backstop.
